1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Student Attendance Management System
Harsha K • Pradhyut • Suhas

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,500
Academic management
Accounts, students, faculty and class assignments.

3
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:19,400
Admin signs in to manage academic records and user accounts.

4
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:23,433
A live overview of students, faculty, sections and attendance sessions.

5
00:00:23,433 --> 00:00:28,033
Student records are linked to classes and home sections.

6
00:00:28,033 --> 00:00:31,100
Faculty accounts and academic departments are managed centrally.

7
00:00:31,100 --> 00:00:36,167
Each subject is assigned a teacher and an enrolled student roster.

8
00:00:36,167 --> 00:00:39,667
Attendance policy
Configure the threshold and verify dashboard changes.

9
00:00:39,667 --> 00:00:45,033
Admin can configure the minimum attendance percentage.

10
00:00:45,033 --> 00:00:49,700
At 80%, the dashboard flags 3 students below the overall threshold.

11
00:00:49,700 --> 00:00:53,633
Restore the institutional threshold to 75% for this demonstration.

12
00:00:53,633 --> 00:00:57,133
Record attendance
Choose a class, mark the roster and save the session.

13
00:00:57,133 --> 00:01:04,133
Faculty signs in with a separate account and a role-specific dashboard.

14
00:01:04,133 --> 00:01:09,467
Select an assigned class, attendance date and teaching period.

15
00:01:09,467 --> 00:01:15,800
Mark S001 Present, S002 Absent and S004 Present.

16
00:01:15,800 --> 00:01:20,467
Save the complete roster. The application confirms success.

17
00:01:20,467 --> 00:01:24,633
Reloading preserves the saved session and all three attendance marks.

18
00:01:24,633 --> 00:01:28,133
Track attendance
View updated percentages and filter the saved record.

19
00:01:28,133 --> 00:01:36,100
The student signs in to see their own attendance and shortage status.

20
00:01:36,100 --> 00:01:41,767
The saved mark updates subject totals and the pooled overall percentage.

21
00:01:41,767 --> 00:01:45,033
Filter by the recorded date to verify the new attendance entry.

22
00:01:45,033 --> 00:01:50,133
Verified: 1 class attended out of 1 held — 100.00%.

23
00:01:50,133 --> 00:01:58,133
GitHub Actions passed: lint, formatting, Django checks and 249 tests.

24
